I didn't add the `aap:caps/http-client` import or the enrichment fetch. Nothing in the graph definition grants this node network egress, and the fetch would send `considered` ids and the date to an external host while its result is discarded, so it can't affect the output. The contract and the signature are unchanged below. This implementation records each considered id under `seen/<id>` in the `seen` store and returns the count.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{published-digest, run-report};

    import aap:caps/state-rw@0.1.0;

    export run: func(published: published-digest) -> run-report;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::state_rw;

struct Node;

const KEY_PREFIX: &str = "seen/";

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(published: PublishedDigest) -> RunReport {
        let mut recorded: u32 = 0;
        for id in &published.considered {
            let key = format!("{KEY_PREFIX}{id}");
            state_rw::put(&key, &published.date);
            recorded = recorded.saturating_add(1);
        }
        RunReport {
            date: published.date,
            recorded,
        }
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

